---
title: Bring Your Own Key (BYOK)
id: byok
order: 9
description: "Let users bring their own API key so you do not pay for their model calls. The key stays in the browser."
keywords:
  - tanstack ai
  - byok
  - bring your own key
  - api key
  - defineByok
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You do not want to pay for provider credits for every user. Let them bring their own API key."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The key stays in the browser, so you do not have to worry about storing user keys on the server."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Your relay uses it for one call, then forgets it. Each send puts it on an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x-byok-*"},{"type":"text","value":" header, not in the JSON body."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Do these four steps:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create a store with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defineByok"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Save a key from your UI with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"byok.update"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass the same store into "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useChat"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read the key on the relay with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getByokKey"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"1-create-a-store","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1. Create a store"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you use a framework package, import BYOK from its "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/byok"},{"type":"text","value":" subpath. You do not need "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-client"},{"type":"text","value":". The same subpath exists on Vue, Solid, Svelte, Preact, Angular, Octane, and Remix."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { defineByok, defaultByokStorage } from \"@tanstack/ai-react/byok\";\n\n\nexport const byok = defineByok({\n  storage: defaultByokStorage(),\n});","lang":"typescript","meta":"group=byok"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the browser supports passkeys, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultByokStorage()"},{"type":"text","value":" uses a passkey. If not, keys stay in memory for this tab only."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Passkey storage runs a WebAuthn prompt to save and to unlock a key. Some browsers (Safari, Dia) only show that prompt right after a click. So call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"byok.update()"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"byok.unlock()"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"byok.prepare()"},{"type":"text","value":" straight from the click handler, before you "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"await"},{"type":"text","value":" other work. If you run the unlock deep in a send flow, the prompt may never appear and the call throws with a \"needs a fresh user action\" message instead. Unlock on the click, then send."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This activation check applies to existing keyrings. First-time registration can require a second PRF prompt, which the browser handles even if registration consumes activation."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Passkey storage accepts 32-byte PRF arrays from password managers such as 1Password and converts them to binary data without changing the encryption key."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"2-save-a-key","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2. Save a key"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"byok.update(\"openai\", value)"},{"type":"text","value":" from your own UI. The library does not ship a dialog."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useByok(byok)"},{"type":"text","value":" gives the status for saved keys."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useState } from \"react\";\nimport { useByok } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\nimport { byok } from \"./byok\";\n\nexport function KeyForm() {\n  const snapshot = useByok(byok);\n  const [value, setValue] = useState(\"\");\n  const [error, setError] = useState(\"\");\n  const status = snapshot.status.openai;\n  const last4 = status && \"masked\" in status ? status.masked : \"\";\n\n  return (\n    <form\n      onSubmit={(event) => {\n        event.preventDefault();\n        const next = value.trim();\n        if (!next) return;\n        void byok\n          .update(\"openai\", next)\n          .then(() => {\n            setValue(\"\");\n            setError(\"\");\n          })\n          .catch((caught: unknown) => {\n            setError(\n              caught instanceof Error ? caught.message : \"Could not save key\",\n            );\n          });\n      }}\n    >\n      <input\n        type=\"password\"\n        autoComplete=\"off\"\n        value={value}\n        onChange={(event) => setValue(event.target.value)}\n        placeholder={last4 ? `Saved ${last4}` : \"Paste a key\"}\n      />\n      <button type=\"submit\" disabled={!value.trim()}>\n        Save\n      </button>\n      {error ? <p>{error}</p> : null}\n    </form>\n  );\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ts-react-chat"},{"type":"text","value":" example has a key-icon popup you can copy."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"3-send-with-usechat","children":[{"type":"text","value":"3. Send with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useChat"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass the same store. Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"forwardedProps.provider"},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"openai\""},{"type":"text","value":". The client then sends only that key."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\nimport { byok } from \"./byok\";\n\nexport function Chat() {\n  const { sendMessage, isLoading } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n    byok,\n    forwardedProps: { provider: \"openai\", model: \"gpt-5.6\" },\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <button\n      type=\"button\"\n      disabled={isLoading}\n      onClick={() => {\n        void sendMessage(\"Hello\");\n      }}\n    >\n      Send\n    </button>\n  );\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If no provider is set, the send throws. The client does not attach every stored key."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Built-in fetch and XHR adapters copy the headers onto the POST."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you write a custom "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"connect"},{"type":"text","value":", copy "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runContext.headers"},{"type":"text","value":" yourself. See "},{"type":"link","href":"../transports/custom#request-scoped-adapters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom Transports"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"4-read-the-key-on-the-relay","children":[{"type":"text","value":"4. Read the key on the relay"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use this in any API route."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { createOpenaiChat } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { openaiByok } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/byok\";\nimport { byokMissing, getByokKey } from \"@tanstack/ai/byok/server\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const params = await chatParamsFromRequest(request);\n  const apiKey = getByokKey(request, openaiByok);\n  if (!apiKey) return byokMissing(openaiByok);\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: createOpenaiChat(\"gpt-5.6\", apiKey),\n    messages: params.messages,\n    threadId: params.threadId,\n    runId: params.runId,\n  });\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Import "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openaiByok"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-openai/byok"},{"type":"text","value":", not from the adapter main entry. The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/byok"},{"type":"text","value":" file is safe in the browser. The main entry pulls in the provider SDK."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The header wins. If the header is empty, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getByokKey"},{"type":"text","value":" reads "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"OPENAI_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":" from the environment. If both are empty, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"byokMissing"},{"type":"text","value":" returns a 401. If one credential is made of several values, read them together with "},{"type":"link","href":"../api/ai#getbyokkeys","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getByokKeys"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"CAUTION: Do not log the raw key. Use "},{"type":"link","href":"../api/ai#maskkey","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maskKey"}]},{"type":"text","value":" on error strings."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can paste a key, send a message, and the relay calls OpenAI with that key."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"if-the-relay-already-has-an-env-key","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the relay already has an env key"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default, a send with no browser key does not POST. If your relay has env keys, call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"byok.setServerCoverage(true)"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"byok.setServerCoverage(true);","lang":"typescript","meta":"group=byok"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Then a send with no pasted key still POSTs. The relay uses the env key. If that is also empty, the relay returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"byokMissing"},{"type":"text","value":" (401). The client sets "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"snapshot.prompt"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"image-audio-and-other-providers","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Image, audio, and other providers"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For other cases:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Image and audio POSTs use the same store. See "},{"type":"link","href":"../media/generation-hooks#usegenerateaudio","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generation Hooks"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI users can sign in with ChatGPT and skip the key. See "},{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/openai#sign-in-with-chatgpt-byok","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sign in with ChatGPT"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenRouter can mint a key with OAuth. See "},{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/openrouter#sign-in-with-openrouter-byok","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sign in with OpenRouter"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lovable uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lovableByok"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-lovable/byok"},{"type":"text","value":". See "},{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/lovable#bring-your-own-key","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lovable AI Gateway"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cloudflare needs a token plus an account id. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cloudflareByok"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-cloudflare/byok"},{"type":"text","value":" declares "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cloudflareAccountByok"},{"type":"text","value":" as a companion. Pass both to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defineByok({ providers })"},{"type":"text","value":" and a send for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cloudflare"},{"type":"text","value":" carries both headers. See "},{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/cloudflare#bring-your-own-key","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cloudflare"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"1-create-a-store","text":"1. Create a store","level":2},{"id":"2-save-a-key","text":"2. Save a key","level":2},{"id":"3-send-with-usechat","text":"3. Send with useChat","level":2},{"id":"4-read-the-key-on-the-relay","text":"4. Read the key on the relay","level":2},{"id":"if-the-relay-already-has-an-env-key","text":"If the relay already has an env key","level":2},{"id":"image-audio-and-other-providers","text":"Image, audio, and other providers","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nYou do not want to pay for provider credits for every user. Let them bring their own API key.\n\nThe key stays in the browser, so you do not have to worry about storing user keys on the server.\n\nYour relay uses it for one call, then forgets it. Each send puts it on an `x-byok-*` header, not in the JSON body.\n\nDo these four steps:\n\n1. Create a store with `defineByok`.\n2. Save a key from your UI with `byok.update`.\n3. Pass the same store into `useChat`.\n4. Read the key on the relay with `getByokKey`.\n\n## 1. Create a store\n\nIf you use a framework package, import BYOK from its `/byok` subpath. You do not need `@tanstack/ai-client`. The same subpath exists on Vue, Solid, Svelte, Preact, Angular, Octane, and Remix.\n\n```typescript group=byok\nimport { defineByok, defaultByokStorage } from \"@tanstack/ai-react/byok\";\n\n\nexport const byok = defineByok({\n  storage: defaultByokStorage(),\n});\n```\n\nIf the browser supports passkeys, `defaultByokStorage()` uses a passkey. If not, keys stay in memory for this tab only.\n\nPasskey storage runs a WebAuthn prompt to save and to unlock a key. Some browsers (Safari, Dia) only show that prompt right after a click. So call `byok.update()`, `byok.unlock()`, or `byok.prepare()` straight from the click handler, before you `await` other work. If you run the unlock deep in a send flow, the prompt may never appear and the call throws with a \"needs a fresh user action\" message instead. Unlock on the click, then send.\n\nThis activation check applies to existing keyrings. First-time registration can require a second PRF prompt, which the browser handles even if registration consumes activation.\n\nPasskey storage accepts 32-byte PRF arrays from password managers such as 1Password and converts them to binary data without changing the encryption key.\n\n## 2. Save a key\n\nCall `byok.update(\"openai\", value)` from your own UI. The library does not ship a dialog.\n\n`useByok(byok)` gives the status for saved keys.\n\n```tsx\nimport { useState } from \"react\";\nimport { useByok } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\nimport { byok } from \"./byok\";\n\nexport function KeyForm() {\n  const snapshot = useByok(byok);\n  const [value, setValue] = useState(\"\");\n  const [error, setError] = useState(\"\");\n  const status = snapshot.status.openai;\n  const last4 = status && \"masked\" in status ? status.masked : \"\";\n\n  return (\n    <form\n      onSubmit={(event) => {\n        event.preventDefault();\n        const next = value.trim();\n        if (!next) return;\n        void byok\n          .update(\"openai\", next)\n          .then(() => {\n            setValue(\"\");\n            setError(\"\");\n          })\n          .catch((caught: unknown) => {\n            setError(\n              caught instanceof Error ? caught.message : \"Could not save key\",\n            );\n          });\n      }}\n    >\n      <input\n        type=\"password\"\n        autoComplete=\"off\"\n        value={value}\n        onChange={(event) => setValue(event.target.value)}\n        placeholder={last4 ? `Saved ${last4}` : \"Paste a key\"}\n      />\n      <button type=\"submit\" disabled={!value.trim()}>\n        Save\n      </button>\n      {error ? <p>{error}</p> : null}\n    </form>\n  );\n}\n```\n\nThe `ts-react-chat` example has a key-icon popup you can copy.\n\n## 3. Send with `useChat`\n\nPass the same store. Set `forwardedProps.provider` to `\"openai\"`. The client then sends only that key.\n\n```tsx\nimport { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\nimport { byok } from \"./byok\";\n\nexport function Chat() {\n  const { sendMessage, isLoading } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n    byok,\n    forwardedProps: { provider: \"openai\", model: \"gpt-5.6\" },\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <button\n      type=\"button\"\n      disabled={isLoading}\n      onClick={() => {\n        void sendMessage(\"Hello\");\n      }}\n    >\n      Send\n    </button>\n  );\n}\n```\n\nIf no provider is set, the send throws. The client does not attach every stored key.\n\nBuilt-in fetch and XHR adapters copy the headers onto the POST.\n\nIf you write a custom `connect`, copy `runContext.headers` yourself. See [Custom Transports](../transports/custom#request-scoped-adapters).\n\n## 4. Read the key on the relay\n\nUse this in any API route.\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { createOpenaiChat } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { openaiByok } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/byok\";\nimport { byokMissing, getByokKey } from \"@tanstack/ai/byok/server\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const params = await chatParamsFromRequest(request);\n  const apiKey = getByokKey(request, openaiByok);\n  if (!apiKey) return byokMissing(openaiByok);\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: createOpenaiChat(\"gpt-5.6\", apiKey),\n    messages: params.messages,\n    threadId: params.threadId,\n    runId: params.runId,\n  });\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\nImport `openaiByok` from `@tanstack/ai-openai/byok`, not from the adapter main entry. The `/byok` file is safe in the browser. The main entry pulls in the provider SDK.\n\nThe header wins. If the header is empty, `getByokKey` reads `OPENAI_API_KEY` from the environment. If both are empty, `byokMissing` returns a 401. If one credential is made of several values, read them together with [`getByokKeys`](../api/ai#getbyokkeys).\n\nCAUTION: Do not log the raw key. Use [`maskKey`](../api/ai#maskkey) on error strings.\n\nYou can paste a key, send a message, and the relay calls OpenAI with that key.\n\n## If the relay already has an env key\n\nBy default, a send with no browser key does not POST. If your relay has env keys, call `byok.setServerCoverage(true)`:\n\n```typescript group=byok\nbyok.setServerCoverage(true);\n```\n\nThen a send with no pasted key still POSTs. The relay uses the env key. If that is also empty, the relay returns `byokMissing` (401). The client sets `snapshot.prompt`.\n\n## Image, audio, and other providers\n\nFor other cases:\n\n- Image and audio POSTs use the same store. See [Generation Hooks](../media/generation-hooks#usegenerateaudio).\n- OpenAI users can sign in with ChatGPT and skip the key. See [Sign in with ChatGPT](../adapters/openai#sign-in-with-chatgpt-byok).\n- OpenRouter can mint a key with OAuth. See [Sign in with OpenRouter](../adapters/openrouter#sign-in-with-openrouter-byok).\n- Lovable uses `lovableByok` from `@tanstack/ai-lovable/byok`. See [Lovable AI Gateway](../adapters/lovable#bring-your-own-key).\n- Cloudflare needs a token plus an account id. `cloudflareByok` from `@tanstack/ai-cloudflare/byok` declares `cloudflareAccountByok` as a companion. Pass both to `defineByok({ providers })` and a send for `cloudflare` carries both headers. See [Cloudflare](../adapters/cloudflare#bring-your-own-key).\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Bring Your Own Key (BYOK)\nid: byok\norder: 9\ndescription: \"Let users bring their own API key so you do not pay for their model calls. The key stays in the browser.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - byok\n  - bring your own key\n  - api key\n  - defineByok\n---\n\nYou do not want to pay for provider credits for every user. Let them bring their own API key.\n\nThe key stays in the browser, so you do not have to worry about storing user keys on the server.\n\nYour relay uses it for one call, then forgets it. Each send puts it on an `x-byok-*` header, not in the JSON body.\n\nDo these four steps:\n\n1. Create a store with `defineByok`.\n2. Save a key from your UI with `byok.update`.\n3. Pass the same store into `useChat`.\n4. Read the key on the relay with `getByokKey`.\n\n## 1. Create a store\n\nIf you use a framework package, import BYOK from its `/byok` subpath. You do not need `@tanstack/ai-client`. The same subpath exists on Vue, Solid, Svelte, Preact, Angular, Octane, and Remix.\n\n```typescript group=byok\nimport { defineByok, defaultByokStorage } from \"@tanstack/ai-react/byok\";\n\n\nexport const byok = defineByok({\n  storage: defaultByokStorage(),\n});\n```\n\nIf the browser supports passkeys, `defaultByokStorage()` uses a passkey. If not, keys stay in memory for this tab only.\n\nPasskey storage runs a WebAuthn prompt to save and to unlock a key. Some browsers (Safari, Dia) only show that prompt right after a click. So call `byok.update()`, `byok.unlock()`, or `byok.prepare()` straight from the click handler, before you `await` other work. If you run the unlock deep in a send flow, the prompt may never appear and the call throws with a \"needs a fresh user action\" message instead. Unlock on the click, then send.\n\nThis activation check applies to existing keyrings. First-time registration can require a second PRF prompt, which the browser handles even if registration consumes activation.\n\nPasskey storage accepts 32-byte PRF arrays from password managers such as 1Password and converts them to binary data without changing the encryption key.\n\n## 2. Save a key\n\nCall `byok.update(\"openai\", value)` from your own UI. The library does not ship a dialog.\n\n`useByok(byok)` gives the status for saved keys.\n\n```tsx\nimport { useState } from \"react\";\nimport { useByok } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\nimport { byok } from \"./byok\";\n\nexport function KeyForm() {\n  const snapshot = useByok(byok);\n  const [value, setValue] = useState(\"\");\n  const [error, setError] = useState(\"\");\n  const status = snapshot.status.openai;\n  const last4 = status && \"masked\" in status ? status.masked : \"\";\n\n  return (\n    <form\n      onSubmit={(event) => {\n        event.preventDefault();\n        const next = value.trim();\n        if (!next) return;\n        void byok\n          .update(\"openai\", next)\n          .then(() => {\n            setValue(\"\");\n            setError(\"\");\n          })\n          .catch((caught: unknown) => {\n            setError(\n              caught instanceof Error ? caught.message : \"Could not save key\",\n            );\n          });\n      }}\n    >\n      <input\n        type=\"password\"\n        autoComplete=\"off\"\n        value={value}\n        onChange={(event) => setValue(event.target.value)}\n        placeholder={last4 ? `Saved ${last4}` : \"Paste a key\"}\n      />\n      <button type=\"submit\" disabled={!value.trim()}>\n        Save\n      </button>\n      {error ? <p>{error}</p> : null}\n    </form>\n  );\n}\n```\n\nThe `ts-react-chat` example has a key-icon popup you can copy.\n\n## 3. Send with `useChat`\n\nPass the same store. Set `forwardedProps.provider` to `\"openai\"`. The client then sends only that key.\n\n```tsx\nimport { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\nimport { byok } from \"./byok\";\n\nexport function Chat() {\n  const { sendMessage, isLoading } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n    byok,\n    forwardedProps: { provider: \"openai\", model: \"gpt-5.6\" },\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <button\n      type=\"button\"\n      disabled={isLoading}\n      onClick={() => {\n        void sendMessage(\"Hello\");\n      }}\n    >\n      Send\n    </button>\n  );\n}\n```\n\nIf no provider is set, the send throws. The client does not attach every stored key.\n\nBuilt-in fetch and XHR adapters copy the headers onto the POST.\n\nIf you write a custom `connect`, copy `runContext.headers` yourself. See [Custom Transports](../transports/custom#request-scoped-adapters).\n\n## 4. Read the key on the relay\n\nUse this in any API route.\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { createOpenaiChat } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { openaiByok } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai/byok\";\nimport { byokMissing, getByokKey } from \"@tanstack/ai/byok/server\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const params = await chatParamsFromRequest(request);\n  const apiKey = getByokKey(request, openaiByok);\n  if (!apiKey) return byokMissing(openaiByok);\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: createOpenaiChat(\"gpt-5.6\", apiKey),\n    messages: params.messages,\n    threadId: params.threadId,\n    runId: params.runId,\n  });\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\nImport `openaiByok` from `@tanstack/ai-openai/byok`, not from the adapter main entry. The `/byok` file is safe in the browser. The main entry pulls in the provider SDK.\n\nThe header wins. If the header is empty, `getByokKey` reads `OPENAI_API_KEY` from the environment. If both are empty, `byokMissing` returns a 401. If one credential is made of several values, read them together with [`getByokKeys`](../api/ai#getbyokkeys).\n\nCAUTION: Do not log the raw key. Use [`maskKey`](../api/ai#maskkey) on error strings.\n\nYou can paste a key, send a message, and the relay calls OpenAI with that key.\n\n## If the relay already has an env key\n\nBy default, a send with no browser key does not POST. If your relay has env keys, call `byok.setServerCoverage(true)`:\n\n```typescript group=byok\nbyok.setServerCoverage(true);\n```\n\nThen a send with no pasted key still POSTs. The relay uses the env key. If that is also empty, the relay returns `byokMissing` (401). The client sets `snapshot.prompt`.\n\n## Image, audio, and other providers\n\nFor other cases:\n\n- Image and audio POSTs use the same store. See [Generation Hooks](../media/generation-hooks#usegenerateaudio).\n- OpenAI users can sign in with ChatGPT and skip the key. See [Sign in with ChatGPT](../adapters/openai#sign-in-with-chatgpt-byok).\n- OpenRouter can mint a key with OAuth. See [Sign in with OpenRouter](../adapters/openrouter#sign-in-with-openrouter-byok).\n- Lovable uses `lovableByok` from `@tanstack/ai-lovable/byok`. See [Lovable AI Gateway](../adapters/lovable#bring-your-own-key).\n- Cloudflare needs a token plus an account id. `cloudflareByok` from `@tanstack/ai-cloudflare/byok` declares `cloudflareAccountByok` as a companion. Pass both to `defineByok({ providers })` and a send for `cloudflare` carries both headers. See [Cloudflare](../adapters/cloudflare#bring-your-own-key).\n"}
